  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nA warm day will be in place for Wednesday with highs in the upper 80s\nto lower 90s. Some heat index values around the tri-state will be\nnear advisory criteria. There is some uncertainty with cloud cover\nmoving in if this will keep temperatures from reaching criteria,\nhowever either way expect hot conditions and have mention in the HWO.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nA few pop up thunderstorms will be possible into the evening hours\nbefore dissipating this evening. During the day on Wednesday\nthunderstorms are expected to develop in advance of a cold front.\nThere is some uncertainty on where initiation will begin with some \nsolutions showing storms developing and moving into northwest \nportions of the region and other solutions developing thunderstorms \nbeginning generally northwest of Interstate 71. The greatest threat \nis across locations northwest of Interstate 71. There is marginal \nrisk for storms across most of the region except for far southeastern\nportions of the area. \n\nThe severe threat Wednesday afternoon and evening will transition \nover to a flash flood threat overnight Wednesday night into Thursday.\nMoisture transport vectors show a west to east orientation so there \nis some concern that there will be a flood potential if multiple \nstorms move over the same area. Thunderstorm activity will gradually \ntaper off late Thursday into Thursday night. Have both the severe and\nflash flood threat mentioned in the HWO.",
